diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 87352402..ebeefbfb 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -132,6 +132,9 @@ On macOS and Windows, cached history remains stale after reconnecting until a ne
 Disabling a host stops its connection and excludes it from displayed totals while retaining its in-memory history.
 Re-enabling can show that retained history as stale until refreshed; deleting the host or changing its destination clears it.
 When multiple connections report the same machine, history is selected per source; stale or partial status reflects every connection whose history contributes.
+Combined today's average uses valid measured output and duration for each selected machine and source, not a simple
+average of host averages. If a required contribution is unavailable, the combined average is unavailable. Remote
+live reasoning readings use the same semantics as local readings when provided by the collector.
 Fields absent from logs are unknown. Live rates inferred from recent completed responses are estimates; completed
 response rates use the logged duration. On macOS and Windows, the chart's “Estimating” legend remains visible
 whenever the selected range includes a dashed estimated segment, even after that response has completed. In particular omp commonly writes a response when it completes, so remote
@@ -139,10 +142,16 @@ monitoring cannot measure per-token streaming speed or infer an unrecorded time
 the first-token wait. It cannot reveal router retries or account cooldowns absent from the logs.
 
 Remote sources and agents appear alongside local sources in the native dashboard and history when available. Remote
-data does not include categorized today's token totals, project paths, traffic or a continuous live chart; unavailable
-values, including missing price data, remain unknown. History is aggregated in the viewer's time zone, requested by
-the client from the collector. Partial log reads are marked as potentially incomplete. Remote network and performance
-history are unavailable; disconnected intervals remain gaps rather than continuous measurements.
+data does not include categorized today's token totals, project paths or a continuous live chart; unavailable
+values, including missing price data, remain unknown. Network traffic is reported when the collector can observe it.
+History is aggregated in the viewer's time zone, requested by
+the client from the collector. Partial log reads are marked as potentially incomplete. Supported collectors provide
+remote performance scores and host-specific baselines, plus real daily performance history from analyzed logs. A
+baseline uses the collector host's local dates; history uses the viewer's time zone, so day boundaries can differ.
+If a selected host has no performance history, available records remain visible with an incomplete-data notice.
+A known empty performance history is not treated as missing.
+Older collectors without performance fields leave it unavailable while their other data remains usable. Remote network
+history is unavailable, and disconnected intervals remain gaps rather than continuous measurements.
 After the client requests its time zone, snapshot today totals also use that zone. Untagged or null-zone snapshots
 retain collector-local compatibility behavior. History from older collectors without a matching time-zone tag is
 unavailable rather than being mislabeled as viewer-local.
